From 95fa1834b65e34d8a7087861d52625cc16aa63bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Vicory <dvicory@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 22:25:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(terminal): bind environments to trusted task authority

Add an infrastructure-only hook that combines raw task or session identity with
a broker-supplied binding to derive an opaque authority-scoped environment key.
Authority bindings outrank ordinary backend overrides and are absent from model
tool schemas, so model-selected task ids cannot select another sandbox.

Serialize the shared override registry so concurrent CWD or backend updates
cannot discard authority. Preserve the exact pre-spawn environment binding and
board-qualified task-run identity across the worker process boundary, then
remove that binding with the task's remaining override state during cleanup.

Keep this extension separate from secure-terminal-isolation.patch: generic
cross-surface identity and shared-owner cleanup remain backend-independent,
while broker deployments opt into stronger lifecycle fencing.
